Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.15,0:00:36.35,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,My lord, blasphemy!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.35,0:00:39.11,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,This is utter blasphemy!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.11,0:00:40.64,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,He showed no mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.64,0:00:44.46,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,He hanged my nephew and your \Nknight right in front of me!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.20,0:00:48.16,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Your Grace, the knights and I are ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.16,0:00:49.76,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Just give the order!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.76,0:00:51.64,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,We'll raze Border Town to the ground
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.64,0:00:54.34,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,and use that brat's skull \Nas a drinking bowl!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.37,0:01:01.12,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,Is there something you'd like to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.81,0:01:05.92,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Your Grace, this is not merely \Na matter of personal pride.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.92,0:01:08.97,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Doing so would sacrifice the \Nentire population of Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.97,0:01:11.67,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,and inevitably lead to a complete break \Nwith the Graycastle royal family.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.67,0:01:13.01,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Coward!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.01,0:01:16.27,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Are we just going to let \Nthat brat shit all over us?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.88,0:01:19.12,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Your Grace, I understand your anger,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.12,0:01:21.77,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,but now is not the best \Ntime to send our troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.77,0:01:24.65,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Once war starts, our enemy \Nwon't be the Fourth Prince,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.65,0:01:26.46,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,but the entire Graycastle royal family.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.23,0:01:28.52,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.55,0:01:34.72,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,If we must do this, \NI have three suggestions.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.72,0:01:36.90,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,First, implement a scorched-earth policy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.90,0:01:38.24,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Under the pretext of \Nprotecting the people,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.24,0:01:42.04,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,relocate the surrounding population, \Nsupplies, and food into the Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.04,0:01:43.62,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Cut off the Fourth Prince's supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.62,0:01:45.59,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Second, fortify strategic locations.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.59,0:01:47.00,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Sending troops to Border Town
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.00,0:01:49.01,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,would be declaring war on \Nthe Graycastle royal family.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.01,0:01:52.00,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,We must be wary and stem reinforcements\Nsent by First Prince Gerald
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.00,0:01:53.31,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,from Coldwind Ridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.31,0:01:56.10,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Third, prepare our troops for battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.10,0:01:59.00,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,but under the guise of the knights' \Nannual purge of the demonic beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.00,0:02:01.22,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,We must not alert the enemy prematurely.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.22,0:02:03.37,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,The Months of Demons are nearly upon us.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.37,0:02:04.78,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,If we launch an attack now,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.78,0:02:06.76,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,we won't be fully prepared.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.76,0:02:09.14,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Border Town has been preparing for months.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.14,0:02:11.43,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,If we fail to win in one \Nfell swoop and it drags on,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.43,0:02:12.68,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Graycastle will reinforce them,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.68,0:02:14.15,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,and we'll be fighting on two fronts.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.87,0:02:15.82,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Instead,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.92,0:02:18.76,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,wait until after the Months of Demons,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.76,0:02:20.35,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,then send our knights to attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.14,0:02:23.95,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Perhaps we can even attribute \Nthe Fourth Prince's death
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.95,0:02:25.80,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,to the invasion of the demonic beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.07,0:02:28.18,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,We'll do as you say,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.92,0:02:31.89,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,and make all the necessary preparations.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.19,0:02:35.33,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,Either he dies during \Nthe Months of Demons,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.33,0:02:39.27,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,or he dies beneath the \Nhooves of my cavalry!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.77,0:04:43.76,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,So this is the incredibly powerful \Nthing you were talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.76,0:04:46.51,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,It looks like a furnace?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.29,0:04:50.31,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,And it's got some wheels \Nand levers attached.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.16,0:04:52.55,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You'll see in a moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.38,0:04:55.55,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Miss Anna, light the fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.27,0:04:56.81,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.31,0:05:02.81,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Th-This is... boiling water?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.46,0:05:05.01,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,So it really is a furnace.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.01,0:05:05.87,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.87,0:05:09.81,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's just a furnace with some \Nwheels and metal levers.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.81,0:05:13.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The key is that they're assembled \Naccording to a certain principle.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.18,0:05:15.21,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Principle?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.76,0:05:17.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This is what I told you before,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.50,0:05:19.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,the power hidden within nature:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.09,0:05:21.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,the power of steam!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.81,0:05:24.67,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,As long as we master that principle,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.67,0:05:27.13,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,even the tiniest forces in nature
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.13,0:05:30.34,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,can be harnessed together \Nand become unstoppable!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.75,0:05:41.75,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness, what is this thing called?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.75,0:05:44.58,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I call it a steam engine.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.58,0:05:47.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This is the first one, \Nso let's just call it Steam Engine #1.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.68,0:05:49.27,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Steam Engine #1.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.27,0:05:52.00,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Does that mean there will \Nbe a #2 and a #3 later?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.00,0:05:55.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yes. Do you still remember \Nthe welding method?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.18,0:05:57.18,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Yes, leave it to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.18,0:05:58.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.49,0:05:59.42,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.42,0:06:01.18,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Ah, yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.18,0:06:02.38,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.14,0:06:07.18,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, this power \Nis truly astonishing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.18,0:06:09.87,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,You said it can replace \Nhuman and animal labor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.87,0:06:11.68,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Now I believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.68,0:06:13.22,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,With such immense power,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.22,0:06:15.84,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I'm afraid even ten knights \Ncould barely withstand it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.97,0:06:19.66,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Training a qualified knight \Ntakes fifteen years,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.66,0:06:22.39,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,but building one of these \Nfurnaces takes only three days.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.39,0:06:24.64,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Even accounting for the \Ntime to forge the parts,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.64,0:06:26.10,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,it's no more than a week.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.10,0:06:27.80,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, at this rate,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.80,0:06:30.43,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,is there still a need \Nfor us knights to exist?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.43,0:06:31.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,There you go again.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.74,0:06:34.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It will replace horses, not people.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.88,0:06:36.40,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Didn't you say this to me before?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.40,0:06:38.16,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Knighthood is a spiritual legacy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.16,0:06:40.66,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Charging on horseback \Nis just one form of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.66,0:06:42.66,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,A knight will always be a knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.66,0:06:45.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Muskets will replace your bows and spears,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.56,0:06:48.77,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and the steam engine will \Nbecome your new cavalry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.94,0:06:51.34,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.22,0:06:55.12,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Besides, I won't be deploying it\N for military use just yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.12,0:06:57.76,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I plan to use it in \Nthe northern mines first.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.76,0:07:00.69,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It will significantly increase \Nour ore production efficiency.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.69,0:07:02.69,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Combined with Miss Anna's ability,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.69,0:07:05.66,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,our productivity will be vastly improved!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.43,0:07:10.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter, take some men and lay \Nrailway tracks inside the mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.47,0:07:13.24,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Then secure the ropes to the steam engine
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.24,0:07:15.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and send it to work there.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.11,0:07:18.16,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,From now on, we'll use the steam \Nengine to transport the ore.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.16,0:07:19.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This will eliminate manual labor,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.93,0:07:22.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and accelerate production.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.03,0:07:36.78,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Although steam seems gentle,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.78,0:07:38.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,it is actually very dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.47,0:07:40.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,A scald can have dire consequences.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.72,0:07:42.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Therefore, before venting \Nthe steam engine,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.84,0:07:45.76,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,you must issue a loud warning \Nand clear the surrounding area.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.76,0:07:47.44,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,For everyone's safety,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.44,0:07:49.19,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,we must always keep this in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.50,0:08:12.82,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Sister Anna, do you want to have a rest?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.82,0:08:14.86,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Oh, it's fine. I'm coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.38,0:08:20.43,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Sister...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.43,0:08:21.19,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.19,0:08:22.88,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Aren't you scared?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.88,0:08:24.14,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Scared of what?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.72,0:08:26.92,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Demonic possession.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.92,0:08:30.72,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,What Sister Nightingale said \Nfeels so terrifying.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.72,0:08:45.42,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,It's okay. We'll get through it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.00,0:08:47.26,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,I don't know...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.26,0:08:49.33,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,I'm not as strong as you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.49,0:08:52.72,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I'm not really that strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.72,0:08:56.27,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I used to think death was my fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.27,0:09:00.10,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Until... I found a reason\Nto continue living.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.46,0:09:02.85,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,You will definitely find a \Nreason to continue living,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.16,0:09:07.52,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,even if it's only struggling to survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.24,0:09:12.85,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,If only I could help Sister and \NHis Highness with the furnace...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.00,0:09:15.10,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Miss Pine!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.28,0:09:25.85,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Miss Anna, Miss Pine, His Highness \Nrequests your presence immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.85,0:09:27.29,Flashback,Brian,0,0,0,,Someone has been scalded.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.69,0:09:32.49,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,How did this accident happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.49,0:09:34.35,Flashback,Carter,0,0,0,,Nail, the operator of Steam Engine #1,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.35,0:09:37.41,Flashback,Carter,0,0,0,,didn't follow your safety protocols \Nduring the venting procedure.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.41,0:09:39.85,Flashback,Carter,0,0,0,,The foreman, Iron Head, happened \Nto pass through his blind spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.32,0:09:41.71,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,How are his injuries?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.71,0:09:43.85,Flashback,Carter,0,0,0,,Well, extensive burns to his face.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.85,0:09:45.51,Flashback,Carter,0,0,0,,It's very severe.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.51,0:09:47.19,Flashback,Carter,0,0,0,,I'm afraid he won't last the night.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.72,0:09:48.44,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.07,0:09:51.88,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Quick, get Brian to \Nbring Nana to save him!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.88,0:09:52.72,Flashback,Carter,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.72,0:09:54.42,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, please wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.42,0:09:55.85,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,What is it, Barov?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.50,0:09:59.01,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, Brian is loyal,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.01,0:10:01.23,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,but these miners cannot be trusted!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.23,0:10:03.28,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,If we get Miss Pine to use \Nher powers to save him,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.28,0:10:04.84,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,then her identity as a witch,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.84,0:10:08.43,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,and the secret of our having \Nwitches here, will be exposed!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.29,0:10:12.85,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,It's fine. It was bound \Nto happen sooner or later.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.15,0:10:14.77,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Industrialization has just begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.77,0:10:18.30,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,We must not let an accident like this \Nmake the people fear Steam Engine #1.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.66,0:10:20.48,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Save him!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.81,0:10:35.66,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.58,0:10:38.06,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Miss Pine is here!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.06,0:10:40.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nana, come in quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.85,0:10:57.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nana, just like in practice,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.68,0:10:58.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,save him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.64,0:10:59.29,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.22,0:11:00.76,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.76,0:11:01.42,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.58,0:11:12.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's okay. It's just like \Ntreating a small animal.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.72,0:11:14.63,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,You can do it, Nana!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.84,0:11:51.46,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Well done, Nana!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.36,0:11:56.23,Main,Miner,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.71,0:11:57.31,Main,Miner,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.60,0:12:00.07,Main,Nail,0,0,0,,This is demonic power.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.56,0:12:01.31,Main,Nail,0,0,0,,A witch!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.00,0:12:03.35,Main,Nail,0,0,0,,It's a witch!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.35,0:12:07.45,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.45,0:12:08.83,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,So what if she's a witch?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.83,0:12:10.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I don't want to hide \Nthis from you anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.52,0:12:12.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Everything the Church says is a lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.85,0:12:14.65,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Not only are witches harmless,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.65,0:12:16.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,they are our allies!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.80,0:12:19.63,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Witches will stand with us \Nto defend Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.63,0:12:21.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,to defend all of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.02,0:12:23.58,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,What are you still afraid of?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.44,0:12:26.09,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Miss Nana saved his life.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.09,0:12:27.52,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,She saved my life too!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.91,0:12:29.69,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Open your eyes and look!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.69,0:12:32.72,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Has any of us ever been harmed by a witch?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.01,0:12:37.50,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Those who truly harm us \Nare the nobles, and the Church!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.50,0:12:38.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nana!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.50,0:12:40.50,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Nana!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.22,0:12:42.32,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.22,0:12:42.32,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nana!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.32,0:12:43.20,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.20,0:12:44.54,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Bad news, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.81,0:12:49.80,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Miss Pine's father, Baron Tigui Pine, \Nhas stormed into the castle!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.80,0:12:53.60,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,It seems he already knows \Nthat Miss Pine is a witch!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.65,0:12:55.72,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I'll go find Nana.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.08,0:12:58.22,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness, please focus \Non handling this situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.73,0:13:07.03,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'll leave this to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.03,0:13:08.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Talk some sense into them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.18,0:13:10.72,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.64,0:13:15.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Let's go. The inevitable is now upon us.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.89,0:13:17.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Let's go meet him.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.13,0:13:35.51,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Your Highness, where is my daughter?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.85,0:13:40.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you, Baron Pine.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.94,0:13:40.06,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Cut the nonsense!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.96,0:13:43.46,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I know my daughter is here, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.46,0:13:46.14,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Please bring her out immediately \Nand hand her over to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.14,0:13:49.98,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Baron Pine, please maintain the \Nproper etiquette of a noble!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.98,0:13:52.31,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,You are speaking to \NHis Highness the Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.31,0:13:54.22,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I know Nana is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.22,0:13:55.56,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Your Highness's actions
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.56,0:13:58.24,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,have already crossed the line \Nof what a noble can tolerate!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.06,0:14:04.06,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Please hand her over to me right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.06,0:14:04.93,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Guards!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.48,0:14:08.06,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Baron Pine, lower your sword!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.42,0:14:11.91,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Carter Lannis, I've heard much about you,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.91,0:14:14.06,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,but this is not Graycastle!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.92,0:14:18.89,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, be careful!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.14,0:14:29.14,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Baron Pine!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.95,0:14:31.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I understand your position and situation,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.64,0:14:33.65,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,but you are Nana's father, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.65,0:14:35.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,How can you bear to do this?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.36,0:14:38.30,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,It is precisely because I am \Nher father that I must do this!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.30,0:14:40.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Do you know what the \NChurch will do to her?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.18,0:14:42.18,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I don't care what the Church thinks!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.18,0:14:43.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Witches are innocent!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.47,0:14:44.86,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,So what if she's a witch?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.86,0:14:47.34,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I won't let anyone hurt my daughter!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.47,0:14:54.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Did you say... you don't \Ncare that Nana is a witch?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.35,0:14:57.19,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Did you say... witches are innocent?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.18,0:15:05.53,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,So, Your Highness brought Nana \Nto the castle to protect her.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.53,0:15:09.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yes, usually I bring her here to \Ndo some learning and training.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.47,0:15:13.49,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Oh. Please forgive my \Nrudeness, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.49,0:15:15.73,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I-I was too impatient.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.73,0:15:19.21,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I thought Your Highness had \Nfound out that Nana was a witch,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.21,0:15:21.14,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,and sent people to arrest her.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.56,0:15:23.90,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's nothing. Just a misunderstanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.90,0:15:27.92,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,By the way, when did you find \Nout that Nana is a witch?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.92,0:15:31.12,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Well, it's been a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.12,0:15:34.02,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I've been careful to keep it a secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.50,0:15:35.77,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nana.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.46,0:15:43.02,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Nana, come here to Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.74,0:15:45.93,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Will you sell me to the Church?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.93,0:15:50.40,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,What are you saying, silly child?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.40,0:15:53.28,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,The Church wouldn't want a dummy like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.28,0:15:55.44,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Come on, come home with Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.24,0:15:59.56,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.82,0:16:07.53,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,There, there...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.18,0:16:11.02,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I would never give you to anyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.02,0:16:18.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I wasn't the first to \Ndiscover her awakening.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.35,0:16:20.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It was her teacher, Karl van Bate.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.99,0:16:22.75,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Because of his friendship with Anna,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.75,0:16:24.25,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,he entrusted Nana to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.25,0:16:26.32,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,hoping that I could protect her.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.32,0:16:27.66,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And for the past month and a half,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.66,0:16:30.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,she's come to the castle whenever \Nshe's free to practice her ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.00,0:16:33.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oh, right. Nana's ability is healing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.60,0:16:35.99,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Oh, I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.99,0:16:39.15,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,That explains how that cat could \Nsuddenly run and jump again.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.44,0:16:41.89,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,It's nothing, really.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.35,0:16:45.44,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,When I came home, I saw \Nher sitting at the door
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.44,0:16:47.80,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,holding a cat that had \Nbeen hit by a carriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.80,0:16:50.28,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I was going to scare her from behind,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.28,0:16:52.84,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,but then that cat saw me and ran off.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.84,0:16:54.58,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Ran like the wind,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.58,0:16:56.78,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,even though its leg had been broken!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.95,0:17:01.44,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Are you two friends?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.44,0:17:02.40,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.36,0:17:07.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It seems you don't believe witches are \Nevil beings led astray by the Devil.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.27,0:17:10.36,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,My daughter is certainly not evil.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.36,0:17:12.00,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,No matter what she has become,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.00,0:17:13.39,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,there's no doubt about that!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.68,0:17:14.86,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I don't think so either.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.45,0:17:18.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nana's ability means a \Ngreat deal to the wounded.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.93,0:17:23.19,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Baron Pine, you just said you \Nwouldn't give Nana to anyone,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.19,0:17:25.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,but I hope she can stay in Border Town
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.60,0:17:27.79,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,to help me fight against \Nthe Months of Demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.48,0:17:30.98,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Your Highness, forgive me for refusing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.98,0:17:32.40,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Nana is still young,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.40,0:17:34.47,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,and the Months of Demons are so dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.47,0:17:36.22,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I must keep her with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.22,0:17:37.97,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Father, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.64,0:17:38.72,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Stop talking. What do you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.72,0:17:40.93,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,So what if you can heal little animals?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.93,0:17:43.22,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,You're just causing trouble \Nfor His Highness here!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.74,0:17:47.44,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Your Highness, I'm impressed \Nby your open-mindedness,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.44,0:17:50.43,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,but the other townsfolk \Nwon't see it that way!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.80,0:17:54.00,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I really can't let Nana take risks here!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.00,0:17:57.28,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,You should know that right now, \Nthe dangers in Border Town
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.28,0:17:59.27,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,aren't limited to just the demonic beasts!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.27,0:18:00.73,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Let's go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.73,0:18:02.33,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I'll take you to the Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.33,0:18:04.25,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Don't mention this to anyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.25,0:18:05.27,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.56,0:18:09.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.03,0:18:13.49,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Your Highness, the miner \Nwho was injured
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.49,0:18:15.26,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,has something to say to Miss Pine.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.24,0:18:35.00,Main,Iron Head,0,0,0,,Praise be to God!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.31,0:18:39.64,Main,Iron Head,0,0,0,,Miss Pine, thank you for saving my life!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.64,0:18:42.64,Main,Iron Head,0,0,0,,Sir Brian told us everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.03,0:18:45.64,Main,Iron Head,0,0,0,,We were all fooled by the Church before!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.64,0:18:48.64,Main,Iron Head,0,0,0,,It was Miss Pine's \Nwitchcraft that saved us!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.85,0:18:54.18,Main,Iron Head,0,0,0,,I will never forget \NMiss Pine's great kindness!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.22,0:19:04.68,Main,Iron Head,0,0,0,,Miss Pine is my goddess!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.20,0:19:09.66,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,No need to thank me...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.02,0:19:14.22,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,I'm glad I could help everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.25,0:19:18.07,Main,Ironhead,0,0,0,,Miss Pine...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.56,0:19:33.92,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Baron Pine, I hear your title \Nwas inherited from your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.92,0:19:37.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,He was once a knight, \Nand due to valor in battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.22,0:19:39.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,he was granted the title \Nof baron and a fiefdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.52,0:19:41.65,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,That's right, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.24,0:19:45.51,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It was a battle of honor fought \Nto defend the innocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.51,0:19:47.30,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Demonic beasts breached \Nthe Stronghold's defenses
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.30,0:19:48.71,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and entered the heart \Nof the Western Region.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.71,0:19:50.61,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That was your father's sector.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.61,0:19:53.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,He gathered the militia, \Ntook his retainers,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.31,0:19:56.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,fought the demonic beasts \Nhead-on, and won.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.00,0:19:58.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You were there yourself, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.00,0:20:01.28,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Yes, though I was only \Nin my teens back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.28,0:20:03.90,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I followed my father into battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.90,0:20:07.81,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,The lead demonic beast was \Na hybrid, enormous in size,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.81,0:20:09.96,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,like a deer and an ox combined.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.96,0:20:13.14,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Its legs were thicker \Nthan my father's body.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.14,0:20:15.39,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,The ground trembled when it ran.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.70,0:20:21.86,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,That creature's antlers still \Nhang above my fireplace.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.88,0:20:26.24,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Baron Pine,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.24,0:20:29.91,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,you don't seem like a traditional noble.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.91,0:20:34.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Your armor, your sword, \Nand the calluses on your hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.00,0:20:37.04,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The spirit of knighthood \Nstill flows in your blood.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.04,0:20:38.54,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Your Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.54,0:20:41.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This time, I have also \Norganized a militia,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.11,0:20:43.38,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,to defend our homeland \Nand people once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.38,0:20:47.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Baron Pine, I hope you \Nwill fight alongside us!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.41,0:20:54.78,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Then, Your Highness, may I send \NNana back to Longsong Stronghold?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.78,0:20:57.28,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,No one has ever held off \Ndemonic beasts here before.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.28,0:20:59.35,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,If we fail...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.00,0:21:02.62,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Have you considered
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.62,0:21:05.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,what the consequences would be \Nif Nana were discovered to be a witch
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.64,0:21:06.77,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,in Longsong Stronghold?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.77,0:21:07.87,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.56,0:21:10.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You just saw it yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.84,0:21:12.98,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The people of Border Town \Nhave accepted Nana.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.98,0:21:17.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Soon, Nana's name will be \Nspoken of like a guardian angel.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.84,0:21:19.98,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,She is safest here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.77,0:21:22.49,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Border Town will not fall.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.49,0:21:24.10,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,When the Months of Demons arrive,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.10,0:21:26.99,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I will fight alongside my \Npeople on the city wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.99,0:21:30.14,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Our opponents are nothing but \Na pack of mutated beasts,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.14,0:21:32.24,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,not invincible demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.24,0:21:34.97,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Your father once defeated \Nthem on an open plain,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.97,0:21:37.77,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and now we have an impregnable wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.48,0:21:41.92,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If... I mean, if the worst were to happen,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.92,0:21:45.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I would have Nana leave first, \Nalong with Anna.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.59,0:21:51.43,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,In that case, I trust you, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.37,0:21:56.67,Main,Tigui,0,0,0,,I am willing to fight for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.91,0:22:58.22,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Good evening, Anna, Nana.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.05,0:23:00.25,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Sister Nightingale?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.25,0:23:02.08,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I brought some fish cakes. Want some?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.08,0:23:04.22,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Ah, fish cakes!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.85,0:23:07.58,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Nana, remember what His Highness said.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.58,0:23:09.57,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Wash your hands before eating.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.57,0:23:10.80,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Go fetch a wash basin.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.80,0:23:12.15,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Oh, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.56,0:23:31.67,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Anna, are you really not \Ncoming back with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.56,0:23:34.00,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,There are many sisters there.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.00,0:23:36.00,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,They will take good care of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.00,0:23:38.72,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Though supplies are scarce \Nin the Impassable Mountain Range,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.72,0:23:40.42,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,we are all family there,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.42,0:23:42.43,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,gathered together for the same purpose.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.40,0:23:46.80,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,In the Mist, I can see \Nthe contours of magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.80,0:23:49.43,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You have immense magic power \Nlike I've never seen before.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.23,0:23:54.43,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,This winter, I'm afraid you won't \Nmake it through on your own.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.90,0:24:02.24,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Before you became a witch and \Njoined the Cooperation Association,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:02.24,0:24:03.68,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,where did you live?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.22,0:24:11.77,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I... used to live in a \Nbig city to the east,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.77,0:24:13.31,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,not far from Graycastle.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.09,0:24:16.80,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Back then, were you happy?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.34,0:24:21.64,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I used to live in a broken-down \Nhouse next to the old mining area.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.64,0:24:23.87,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,My mother died in a fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.87,0:24:27.54,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,My father sold me out for 25 gold royals.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.38,0:24:30.77,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,It was His Highness who \Nrescued me from that cage.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.77,0:24:32.81,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I am very happy here.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.81,0:24:34.38,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Very fulfilled.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.02,0:24:36.75,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,But you can't leave this castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.67,0:24:39.81,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,We must pursue true freedom!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.81,0:24:42.31,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I am pursuing true freedom!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.64,0:24:46.72,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,If the Holy Mountain is a safe \Nhaven and home for witches,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.26,0:24:50.56,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,then I think I have already \Nfound my Holy Mountain.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:00.18,0:25:01.89,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Sister Anna, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.13,0:25:15.71,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,It's snowing.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.27,0:25:23.19,Sign_Basic,CREDITS,0,0,0,,Translator: Henry Lin\NTimer: Henry Lin\NEditor: Zachary Carlysle\N QC: William Haggard
